 Aufrufe  
20.10.2026
Ten years from now, you could be living better than the richest person on Earth lives today. Not because someone mails you a check, but because AI and robots are about to make almost everything cheap.

In this video: why the scaling laws are pushing AI straight up, why the "few rich people own everything" nightmare is a lot harder to build than it sounds, what already happened in Bangladesh without a single check, the four price killers (making stuff, labor, materials and energy), what has to go right, why we don't feel like kings even though we live better than them, what we'll do with all that time, why the check might come anyway, and what happens when robots start building robots.

Chapters
0:00 Ten years from now
2:43 Why this is happening now
4:41 The nightmare version
6:26 What already happened in Bangladesh
8:20 How things actually get cheap
10:15 What has to go right
11:30 Why we don't feel like kings
13:25 What will still be precious
14:49 What will we do with our time?
17:51 Will the check come anyway?
20:23 What superintelligence could build
21:40 Beyond ten years: when robots build robots
23:32 What to do with the next ten years
24:55 Welcome to the age of abundance

