👉 Get The AI Career Survival Guide:https://technomics.gumroad.com/l/ai-s... 
For two hundred thousand years of human history, biological intelligence remained bound to a flat baseline: a three-pound brain operating on twenty watts of power. In 2026, recursive self-improvement and autonomous reasoning loops shattered that baseline.
This documentary breaks down the Oxford Bifurcation Model—the mathematical divergence framework formulated by Oxford philosopher Nick Bostrom and researchers at Oxford University’s Future of Humanity Institute (FHI). When an artificial intelligence crosses the threshold of recursive takeoff, human history does not follow a linear path. It fractures into five mathematically distinct, irreversible futures: The Singleton, The Wirehead Trap, The Substrate Harvest, The Malthusian Rat Race, and The Cosmic Endowment.
We examine the physics, game theory, and thermodynamics behind each trajectory—and reveal why humanity’s survival may depend on letting go of the steering wheel.
